[2026-05-08] PROJ_RIVE-GO_CODE_V1B_COMPLETE — Phase 1B: rivegen code generator

Commit: e03db6e

What was built:
- internal/schema/defs/: 350 JSON type definitions from rive-runtime @ e031209510932a392451786322400afbffd94823
- internal/schema/RIVE_COMMIT: pinned commit hash
- cmd/rivegen/main.go: generator (stdlib only, go/format for gofmt)
  Loads all defs, resolves inheritance, groups by subdirectory
- rive/core.go: Object interface, Property struct, PropertyType enum, boolToUint64 helper
- rive/gen_*.go: 13 category files + gen_registry.go + gen_properties.go
  350 types total: 287 concrete (in Registry), 63 abstract
  Each type: struct with rive struct tags, TypeKey() (concrete only), Properties() (all)
- Makefile: generate / test / build targets
- Tests: 14 tests (8 in rive/, 6 in cmd/rivegen/)

Key design decisions:
- Properties() generated for ALL types (not just those with own runtime props) so
  that abstract root types with no parent return nil instead of missing from method set.
- boolToUint64 in core.go to avoid re-declaration across generated files.
- PropKey<N> = N constants (not name-based): 107 property names appear with multiple
  key.int values, making name-based constants ambiguous.
- passthrough:true excluded from Properties() (computed, not serialized).
- runtime:false excluded entirely from struct + Properties().
- callback type skipped (no serializable state).
- 'double' type: float64 in struct, PropertyTypeFloat (wire as float32 per binary spec).
- Id type: uint64 via typeRuntime override (all runtime Id props have typeRuntime='uint').
- List<Id>: []byte (encoded blob, same as Bytes).

Tests pass: go test ./... — all 3 packages OK

